# P7 Cutoff boundary 3-state verification — keliya synthetic
# Issue #100 Task 8.10a (split-delivery PR feat/issue-100-s2-p7-gates-partial)
================================================================================

Spec authority:
    openspec/changes/s2-strict-omp-full/specs/p7-final-fusion-omp-cutoff/spec.md
    Requirement L21 "Cutoff serial fallback when NumEle < SHUD_OMP_CUTOFF"
    Scenario L36-L43 "Cutoff strict-less-than semantics at NumEle = 1023 / 1024 / 1025 boundary"

Purpose:
    Verify the runtime cutoff guard `NumEle < shud_omp_cutoff_value()` at
    MD_rhs_core.cpp:624 implements STRICT-LESS-THAN semantics by synthesizing
    a 3-state boundary on keliya (NumEle=484). The (NumEle, cutoff) pair
    (484, 483 / 484 / 485) is isomorphic to the deployed boundary
    (1024, 1023 / 1024 / 1025) under the differential-sign set {>0, ==0, <0}
    that the strict-less-than comparison depends on (spec L43).

    Equivalence rationale (spec L43): cutoff guard is a pure integer compare
    `NumEle < SHUD_OMP_CUTOFF`. The decision only depends on the sign of
    `NumEle - SHUD_OMP_CUTOFF` (one of >0, ==0, <0). Synthesizing the 3-state
    boundary on keliya validates the dispatch logic without requiring a
    NumEle = 1024 case.

