------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Verdict
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  VERDICT: PASS

  Spec L36-L43 "Cutoff strict-less-than semantics at NumEle = 1023 / 1024 /
  1025 boundary" Scenario satisfied:

  - cutoff=485 (NumEle < cutoff)   -> serial fallback         OK
  - cutoff=484 (NumEle == cutoff)  -> serial fallback         OK (strict-less-than)
  - cutoff=483 (NumEle > cutoff)   -> parallel region entered OK

  All 5 runs produced bitwise-identical keliya.rivqdown.dat (SHA256 ==
  b23e15b94c0f67becbf73a45ea08e84f62680614e85e9a9ac15eac6033a51a1a).

  The cutoff=483 multi-thread case (2 + 4 threads) achieving bitwise match
  is STRONGER than the brief minimum requirement: brief said "may DIFFER
  (legitimate; A3b ULP-level expected, not bitwise A3a)". The owner-local
  gather refactor under P1-P6 (#82..#99) eliminated cross-thread FP reorder
  for keliya at the threads tested here. The cross-thread A3b ULP gate for
  CASES with NumEle > OMP_CUTOFF (qinyijiang, heihe_x4) is task 8.10 (split
  to sub-issue #100b) — keliya is not an A3b case per spec
  strict-omp-acceptance-gates §D13 (excluded because NumEle < default
  cutoff 1024; under SHUD_OMP_CUTOFF=483 synthetic it is force-included
  here just for the 3-state dispatch verification, not for ULP gating).

  CVODE stats consistency across all 5 runs:
    nst = 111272, nfe = 112921, nfeLS = 117336, nni = 112920,
    nsetups = 0, netf = 4, npe = 0, nps = 0, ncfn = 276, ncfl = 100
  (identical CVODE step trajectory across all 5 runs confirms the bitwise
  SHA256 match is not a coincidence on the rivqdown.dat slice.)

